# What `docker build` and `gcloud builds submit` send as the build context. The build needs only go.mod, go.sum, cmd/ and
# internal/; keep everything else, above all keys and secrets, out of the builder layer and out of the upload.
# (Patterns here are relative to the root of the context: use **/ to match at any depth.)
.git
.github
.claude
bin
coverage.out
docs
examples
deploy/helm

# Keys, secrets and credentials that the README's quick start or a deployment creates next to the code.
keys
agents
**/*.identity.json
**/*.key
**/*.pem
**/*.p12
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.secret
**/alarm-secret*
**/*.token
**/*-sa.json
**/*sa-key*.json
**/*service-account*.json
**/application_default_credentials.json
**/client_secret*.json
**/credentials*.json

# Terraform (never part of the image)
deploy/terraform
**/.terraform
**/*.tfstate*
**/*.tfvars
